\end{align}
where the last line follows from orthogonality of a projection with its residuals (Lemma \ref{lem:projections}(i)). \\

Now we analyze the bias terms \eqref{eq:mainbias2} and \eqref{eq:covbias2} separately; the first is the main bias term, which would arise even if the covariate density were known, and the second is the contribution coming from having to estimate the covariate density. \\

Recall from \eqref{eq:smallbias} in the main text that if $g$ is $\alpha$-smooth, then 
